The Security Council,

Guided by the purposes and principles of the Charter of the United Nations,

Expressing grave concern over the escalation of violence and the deterioration of the situation in the region, in particular the resulting heavy civilian casualties,

Emphasizing that the civilian population in Israel and the occupied Palestinian territory must be protected, in accordance with international humanitarian law,

Deeply concerned by the worsening humanitarian crisis in the Gaza Strip and its grave impact on the civilian population,

1. Calls for an immediate, durable and fully respected humanitarian ceasefire;

2. Strongly condemns all violence and hostilities directed against civilians and all acts of terrorism;

3. Calls for the secure release of all hostages;

4. Calls for the unhindered provision and distribution of humanitarian assistance, including of food, fuel and medical treatment, as well as the creation of conditions for the safe evacuation of civilians in need;

5. Decides to remain seized of the matter.

The Security Council,

Guided by the purposes and principles of the Charter of the United Nations,

Expressing grave concern over the escalation of violence and the deterioration of the situation in the region, in particular the resulting heavy civilian casualties,

Emphasizing that the civilian population in Israel and the occupied Palestinian territory must be protected, in accordance with international humanitarian law,

Recalling that all parties to the conflict must comply strictly with their obligations under international humanitarian law, including the Geneva Conventions of 1949, and uphold the principles of distinction, precaution, and proportionality,

Deeply concerned by the catastrophic and worsening humanitarian crisis in the Gaza Strip and its grave impact on the civilian population,

1. Calls for an immediate, durable and fully respected humanitarian ceasefire;

2. Strongly condemns all violence and hostilities directed against civilians and all acts of terrorism;

3. Calls for the immediate and unconditional release of all hostages, demanding their safety, well-being and humane treatment in compliance with international law;

4. Calls for the rescission of the order for civilians and United Nations staff to evacuate all areas in northern Gaza;

5. Urges the continuous, sufficient and unhindered provision and distribution of essential goods and humanitarian assistance to civilians, including water, electricity, fuel, food and medical supplies, across the Gaza Strip, as well as the creation of conditions for the safe evacuation of civilians in need;

6. Decides to remain seized of the matter.

